##Task A6:
The model is the most confused between coat and shirt
The images are converted into a sheet of pixels (grayscale images). The model learns from the labelled training dataset(supervised).
Then it tries to predict the label for the images in the test dataset. It is observed that it gets confused b/w some of the images.

In order to overcome this issue, make it more efficient and fix this for production, we can add more training data to the model. This helps it so that it 
improvises by recognising the patterns in the images very well. Coloured images will make it easier for the model to predict. In grayscale, even humans might get confused. 
  
##Stretch:
Reduces Overfitting: When training data is limited, models often memorize specific details or noise rather than learning generalizable patterns.
Augmentation acts as a regularizer, showing the model slightly different versions of the same image so it cannot simply "memorize" a fixed set of pixels.
  (Got the advantage of augmentation from Gemini)









